{
  "raw": {
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:964405/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in snow and microclimate processes of cold-climate ecosystems",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher in snow and microclimate processes of cold-climate ecosystems Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral Researcher in snow and microclimate processes of cold-climate ecosystems Login and apply Faculty of Technology, Water, Energy and Environmental Engineering The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Postdoctoral Researcher in snow and microclimate processes of cold-climate ecosystems for a 3-year fixed-term position to join us in the Faculty of Technology, Water, Energy and Environmental Engineering Unit. About the job We are seeking a postdoctoral researcher to join our team to study changes and patterns in hydrology, snow and microclimates across Arctic, boreal and alpine ecosystems, and to connect their dynamics to ecological processes in cold climates. We welcome applicants with backgrounds in hydrology, remote sensing, data science, physical geography, environmental science, ecosystem science or ecology, as long as you bring strong numerical and programming skills and a genuine interest in cold-climate systems. We recognise that excellent candidates come from different scientific traditions. We therefore invite applications along two complementary profiles, and encourage you to indicate in your application which profile best matches your interests and expertise. Both profiles are equally valued and will be assessed on their own merits. We also welcome candidates whose expertise and interests fall between these profiles or combine elements of both. Profile A — Snow, climate and remote sensing (technical / modelling focus). You will study snow-related processes and the impacts of climate change on them in Arctic, boreal and alpine ecosystems by combining remote sensing tools, microclimate datasets and mechanistic models. You will utilise and develop advanced mechanistic and deep-learning models with fine-resolution satellite imagery and empirical microclimate data to understand and predict the localised effects of climate change and human impacts on cold-climate hydrology and snow. This profile suits a hydrological modeller or data scientist with a strong background in spatial datasets and analyses and deep understanding in cold-climate processes. Profile B — Snow, microclimate and ecosystems (interdisciplinary focus). You will study the dynamics and spatial patterns in snow and hydrological and microclimate conditions and link them to ecological processes in Arctic, boreal and alpine ecosystems. You will investigate how shifts in snow cover, local hydrology and microclimates propagate through cold ecosystems affecting vegetation, biodiversity and ecosystem functions. This profile suits a hydrologist, physical geographer, ecosystem scientist or ecologist with strong numerical and programming skills and an understanding of cold-ecosystem processes and nature. The position is linked to a project led by Assistant Professor Pekka Niittynen that studies local-scale trends in snow cover duration and their ecological implications across Arctic and alpine ecosystems. The postdoctoral position is also linked to large-scale and long-term research in the water sector at the Flagship DIWA - Digital Waters , and SAFIRE - Safeguarding Biodiversity through Interdisciplinary Research on Habitat Restoration- a Profi8 programme at the University of Oulu, funded by the Research Council Finland. SAFIRE’s focus is the production of scientifically excellent and actionable knowledge on habitat restoration, especially in Arctic regions. The position is located at the Water, Energy and Environmental Engineering research unit, in the Faculty of Technology. Our water research team includes 5 research groups with a strong focus on various aspects of water engineering, including hydrological modelling, cold climate hydrology, hydrological process studies, and groundwater research. In hydrology, the research includes studies at our research stations and supersites in Finland with a unique and developing infrastructure. The position is also linked to the Arctic, Antarctic and Mountain initiative , a network of ~150 researchers across the world that works on global microclimate datasets and promotes microclimate research across disciplines. Your responsibilities The responsibilities below are tailored to your chosen profile, with shared responsibilities common to both. Shared responsibilities: Integrate remote sensing observations, climate reanalysis and microclimate data to reconstruct historical snow, hydrological and microclimate trends. Collaborate with ecologists, hydrologists and modellers to assess the impacts of hydrological and cryospheric changes on ecosystems and water resources. Publish high-quality research and contribute to open-source tools. Depending on personal interest, field work in northern Finland, Sweden and Norway is possible. Participate in doctoral supervision and education. In addition, for Profile A: Develop algorithms for fine-scale snow and hydrological mapping and modelling utilising Landsat, Sentinel and PlanetScope satellite data. Advance mechanistic, deep-learning or hybrid models that translate satellite and microclimate data into predictions of snow and hydrological change. In addition, for Profile B: Analyse how changes in snow, hydrology and microclimate propagate to ecological processes in Arctic and alpine tundra and boreal forests. Bridge physical environmental data and model outputs with ecological and biodiversity datasets and outcomes. What we offer We offer you an interesting and versatile position as part of a large and growing digital water research cluster in Finland and the SAFIRE profiling research team. We help you to grow and realise your full scientific potential and contribution. You will have the opportunity to develop professionally with the help of an experienced and enthusiastic team. You will also have access to our unique global infrastructure, where innovative studies can be initiated in collaboration with our team members. The University of Oulu offers Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits. Development and career options of the big organization. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us . Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu. Who are you? To succeed in the position, you are required to have: A relevant doctoral degree in hydrology, remote sensing, data science, environmental science, ecosystem science, ecology, physical geography or a related field. The doctoral degree must have been completed by the closing date for applications. The degree must have been obtained no more than 10 years ago. Ability to engage in independent scientific research. Teaching skills required for the position. Strong background in numerical modelling and data analysis. Experience with programming languages such as R, Python, Julia, Fortran or C/C++. Excellent written and spoken English. Ability to work independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team. Strong experience in scientific writing and excellent communication skills. We also appreciate the following: Experience with satellite remote sensing data and analyses. Experience with collecting and analysing drone imagery. Understanding of cold-ecosystem processes and nature, and experience linking environmental drivers to ecological or biodiversity outcomes. Experience with ecological, hydrological or microclimate field measurements in cold regions. Familiarity with high-performance computing and environments. Experience in supervision or co-supervision of doctoral researchers. International experience and networking skills. Experience in proposal writing. When assessing the candidate's merits for the position of Postdoctoral Researcher, attention will be paid to scientific excellence, such as research outputs, international scientific activities and collaboration, supervision of undergraduate students, pedagogical competence, societal relevance, impact and potential of scientific activities, and services for the academic community, as well as prior experience in working with cold-climate topics. Salary The position is a fixed-term position for 3 years, beginning on 1.12.2026 (or as soon as possible thereafter). A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. The salary will be based on the level 5-6 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities, depending on your qualifications. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). Typical monthly salary for a post-doctoral researcher is 3700 - 4800 € (before taxes), depending on your experience and qualifications. How to apply? Apply online at the latest by October 15, 2026 (23:59 Finnish time). The application should be written in English and include the following documents: A letter of motivation containing a short description of the research you propose to conduct in the position (max 2 pages) An academic Curriculum Vitae (max 4 pages) following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity List of 10 most important publications : select maximum of 10 scientific articles that highlight your research interests and competence and explain your role in them. Teaching and supervision experience (2 pages) Eligible applicants best fitting the expected research profile may be invited to an on-site or remote interview. All applicants will be notified when the selection process is completed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Further information Assistant Professor Pekka Niittynen, pekka.niittynen@oulu.fi Associate Professor Hannu Marttila, hannu.marttila@oulu.fi Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/551 Published 16.Sep.2026 Last application date 15.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:968536/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher, Science and Technology Studies (STS) and aquatic restoration in the Nordic and Arctic regions",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher, Science and Technology Studies (STS) and aquatic restoration in the Nordic and Arctic regions Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral Researcher, Science and Technology Studies (STS) and aquatic restoration in the Nordic and Arctic regions Login and apply Faculty of Humanities, History, Culture and Communication Studies The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are looking to hire highly motivated Postdoctoral Researcher to join the Department of Anthropology, in the History, Culture and Communications Unit at the Faculty of Humanities, the University of Oulu. The hired researcher will develop and implement their own research plan in the specified research area and work in collaboration with Dr. Jose A. Cañada and their research team under the programme “Safeguarding biodiversity through interdisciplinary research on habitat restoration” (SAFIRE). Aquatic ecosystems are a central element in how humans are addressing their own survival. Lakes, rivers, wetlands, seas, oceans and melting ice caps are central elements of the ongoing ecological crisis linked to human modes of economic and capitalist production. Discourses and practices of ecological repair coexist with refusals to give up on ideals of economic growth, often featuring techno-optimist visions to develop possible solutions. In this context, restoration of aquatic habitats has emerged with force as a dominant strategy for environmental care, with links to more traditional conservation approaches or more intrusive geoengineering initiatives. The researcher hired will have the opportunity to develop their own research plan to study how the relation between humans and their surrounding environments is shifting as the result of alterations to aquatic ecologies in the Arctic and Nordic regions, with a special focus on knowledge production and practices from technoscientific, regulatory, citizen, and indigenous perspectives. Social research in this area is key to ensure responsible technoscientific development, and socio-ecologically just development of policy and governance. The position benefits from the University of Oulu’s long-term development of trans- and interdisciplinary research about human-environment relations, currently under the programme “Safeguarding biodiversity through interdisciplinary research on habitat restoration” (SAFIRE). As a result, the hired researcher will be an active participant in the exciting calendar of interdisciplinary activities and events. More information about SAFIRE and its research themes can be found here . About the job Hired researcher will work closely with Dr Jose A. Cañada and their research team. The group is conceived as a site for close collaboration among likeminded researchers that also fosters independence and career development. Dynamics of the group build on the CSSM model for distributed and less hierarchical academic collaboration (learn more here ). The team is formed around a common interest in aquatic ecologies and perspectives in the social sciences on care, participation, methodological experimentation, and justice. These areas of interest are articulated around four thematic areas, which all originate in scholarship in the area of Science and Technology Studies: Thematic area 1: A more-than-human approach based on care that serves as a frame diverse practices for environmental management. In this context, management emerges as a form of interaction that requires close contact with other species and habitats. These are practices that are carried out by a variety of actors, including scientific practitioners, environmental managers, governments, civil society organizations, private sector, citizens, and more. Thematic area 2: A broad understanding of knowledge production with an emphasis on flows manifested through practices and discourses that contribute to diverse and situated accounts of the world that do not fit the universalist and positivist approaches that have historically dominated modern science. Knowledge is understood not as fact discovery but as a collective endeavour that takes place across different societal areas and involves human and nonhuman actors. Thematic area 3: Scientific citizenship and public participation in the production of environmental and aquatic futures through hybrid citizen and scientific communities involved in different strategies to know and care for aquatic habitats. This entails understanding the intersectional positioning and situated contributions of different actors, including not just citizen participation in scientific initiatives but the citizen status of experts and interested parties with specific positions towards socioecological debates. Thematic area 4: Methodological experimentation and sensory approaches to develop new lenses and techniques able to yield different results that do not reify normative understandings which, in some cases, can stagnate and polarize environmental debates. This involves relying on modes of knowledge production that step away but continue to engage with scientific methods developed around notions of validity and reliability. The primary duties will include: Planning and conducting social scientiﬁc research on aquatic ecologies that directly engages with at least two of the four thematic areas mentioned above. Participating of and contributing to internal research group activities; planning and implementing collaboration with group colleagues. Producing academic contributions in the form of e.g. articles, monographs, experimental non-textual formats. Active participation and facilitation of interdisciplinary work both in the context of SAFIRE activities and in their own projects. Participating in outreach initiatives that engage both academic and non-academic publics. Engaging in writing and submitting applications for further research funding. Other administrative and community activities linked to academic life at the University of Oulu. What we offer The support of an experienced and enthusiastic team, with whom you can share your expertise and grow as an expert. Development and career options of the big organization. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being, and flexible multi-location and remote work opportunities in Finland. Read more about other staff benefits. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu . Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. Work that matters! Read more about working with us. Who are you? In order to succeed and enjoy the position, we require from you: Doctoral degree in a relevant field (science and technology studies, anthropology, sociology, social psychology, environmental social sciences, or equivalent) . The doctoral degree must have been completed by the closing date for applications. The degree must have been obtained no more than 10 years ago. An interest in issues related to environmental management of aquatic habitats in the Nordic and/or Arctic regions Experience in qualitative social scientiﬁc research evidenced by peer-reviewed publications or defended doctoral thesis monograph A transdisciplinary research orientation, with experience of or interest in knowledge communities beyond the social sciences and humanities Capacity to collaborate in research and research dissemination activities Excellent written and interpersonal communication skills in English (the working language of the research team) Proven teamwork skills and commitment to academic collaboration We also appreciate: Conversational level of Finnish When assessing the candidate’s merits for the position of Postdoctoral Researcher, attention will be paid to scientific excellence, such as research outputs, international scientific activities and collaboration, supervision of undergraduate students, pedagogical competence, societal relevance, impact and potential of scientific activities, and services for the academic community. Salary The position is fixed-term for 3 years as of 2nd November 2026 (or as agreed). The salary will be based on the levels 5-6 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary will be approx. 3700-4300 € per month (before taxes). A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 30th September 2026 (23:59 Finnish local time) through our recruitment system. The application should be written in English and include the following: Letter of motivation (max. 1 page) summarizing your professional experience and expertise and describing why you are interested in the position Research concept paper (max. 2 pages; references do not count towards this limit) for a potential project in the topic of the position. The plan should include a section that discusses its engagement with at least two of the four thematic areas mentioned above Curriculum vitae (max. 4 pages) in accordance with the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity List of publications , following the guidelines of the Research Council of Finland , with up to five key publications relevant to the position marked in bold Contact information of two to three senior/experienced researchers who may be asked to give a personal statement about you The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. The shortlisted candidates will also be asked to submit their diplomas, and their references will be contacted. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact Dr. Jose A. Cañada (Jose.Canada(at)oulu.fi). Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/570 Published 16.Sep.2026 Last application date 30.Sep.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:968632/": {
      "title": "Yliopisto-opettaja, pohjoissaame",
      "description": "Yliopisto-opettaja, pohjoissaame Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Yliopisto-opettaja, pohjoissaame Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Humanistinen tiedekunta, Giellagas-instituutti Oulun yliopisto on monitieteinen, kansainvälisesti toimiva tiedeyliopisto, jonka noin 4000 työntekijää tuottavat korkeatasoiseen tutkimukseen pohjautuvaa uutta tietoa ja antavat tutkimukseen perustuvaa opetusta kestävämmän, älykkäämmän ja inhimillisemmän maailman rakentamiseksi. Oulun yliopistoyhteisössä toimii kaikkiaan noin 19 000 henkilöä. Pohjoisen tiedeyhteisömme toiminta on globaalisti vaikuttavaa ja luo edellytyksiä innovaatioiden syntymiselle. Kaikkea tutkimus-, opetus- ja työyhteisötoimintaamme ohjaavat yliopistomme arvot sekä eettiset periaatteet. Haemme nyt Oulun yliopiston humanistisen tiedekunnan Giellagas-instituuttiin Yliopisto-opettajaa toistaiseksi voimassa olevaan työsuhteeseen 1.1.2027 lähtien. Giellagas-instituutilla on valtakunnallinen vastuu saamen kielten ja saamelaisen kulttuurin ylimmästä opetuksesta ja tutkimuksesta Suomessa. Instituutin saamen kielten oppiaine kouluttaa kielen asiantuntijoita saamelaisyhteisön tarpeisiin. Opinnot tarjoavat mahdollisuuksia kansainväliseen uraan Pohjoismaiden rajat ylittävällä saamelaisalueella. Saamen kielten opinnoissa on kolme linjaa: pohjoissaamen, inarinsaamen ja koltansaamen linja. Pohjoissaamen linja on tarkoitettu äidinkielisille puhujille sekä muille, joilla on hyvä pohjoissaamen taito. Lisäksi instituutissa voi suorittaa 25 opintopisteen laajuiset pohjoissaamen perusopinnot vieraana kielenä. Työtehtävät Yliopisto-opettajana opetat perus-, aine- ja syventäviä opintoja ohjaat ja tarkastat opinnäytetöitä ohjaat opiskelijoita ja neuvot opintoihin liittyvissä asioissa tutkit pohjoissaamen kieltä osallistut hallinnollisten tehtävien hoitoon Mitä tarjoamme? Tuen asiantuntevalta ja innostavalta Giellagas-instituutin työyhteisöltä, jossa pääset kehittymään ja jakamaan asiantuntemustasi. Liikunta-, kulttuuri- ja hyvinvointietuja (ePassi). Lue lisää muista työsuhde-eduistamme . Ison organisaation tarjoamat kehitys- ja uramahdollisuudet. Merkityksellisen työn ja toimintakulttuurin, jossa sinulla on vapaus työn ja muun elämän yhteensovittamiseen. Lisätietoa työskentelystä Oulun yliopistossa . Mitä etsimme? Onnistuaksesi ja viihtyäksesi tehtävässä edellytämme sinulta: Ylempää korkeakoulututkintoa saamen kielten alalta C2-tasoista kirjallista ja suullista pohjoissaamen taitoa Hyvää opetustaitoa Valmiutta tieteelliseen työhön Sujuvaa kirjallista ja suullista suomen kielen taitoa Lisäksi katsomme eduksi: Pedagoginen koulutus Laaja tehtäväalueen osaaminen Muut opetustoimessa saavutetut ansiot Yliopisto-opettajan odotetaan suorittavan kahden vuoden kuluessa työsuhteen alkamisesta vähintään 25 opintopistettä yliopistopedagogisia tai niihin rinnastettavia opintoja, ellei valitulla ole näitä opintoja suoritettuna työsuhteen alkaessa. Palkkaus Tehtävä on toistaiseksi voimassa oleva alkaen 1.1.2027 (tai sopimuksen mukaan). Tehtävä sijoittuu yliopiston palkkausjärjestelmän opetus- ja tutkimushenkilöstön vaativuustasolle 5. Lisäksi maksetaan henkilökohtaiseen suoriutumiseen perustuvaa palkanosaa, joka on enintään 50 % tehtäväkohtaisesta palkanosasta. Palkka vastaavissa tehtävissä on tyypillisesti 3800-4100 EUR/kk. Tehtävässä sovelletaan 6 kuukauden koeaikaa. Kuinka hakea? Jos kiinnostuit, haethan paikkaa rekrytointijärjestelmän kautta viimeistään 18.10.2026 . Liitä hakemukseen mukaan: Hakemuskirje CV Narratiivinen CV käyttäen annettua mallia (lisätietoja Tutkimuksen ja tutkijan arvioinnin periaatteet Oulun yliopistossa ) Julkaisuluettelo Suomen Akatemian pohjan mukaan Opetusportfolio , Oulun yliopiston ohjeiden mukaisesti Tehtävään parhaiten soveltuvat hakijat kutsutaan haastatteluun, joka pidetään etäyhteydellä tai kasvokkain. Opetustaitoa arvioidaan opetusportfolion ja opetusnäytteen perusteella. Opetustaidon arvioinnista on saatava vähintään arvosana ”hyvä” (3/5). Tulemme olemaan yhteydessä kaikkiin hakijoihin hakuprosessin aikana. Lisätietoja Jäikö jokin arveluttamaan? Ota yhteyttä: johtaja Sigga-Marja Magga, humanistinen tiedekunta, Giellagas-instituutti, sigga-marja.magga@oulu.fi, +358 50 568 5326 Sámegillii ohcamuša sáhttá lohkat dáppe. Työsuhdemuoto Toistaiseksi Työsuhteen luonne Kokoaikainen Paikkojen lukumäärä 1 Työllisyysaste 100% Paikkakunta Oulu Maakunta Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Maa Suomi Ilmoitusnumero 2026/573 Julkaistu 21.09.2026 Haku päättyy 18.10.2026 Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Jaa linkki Takaisin avoimiin työpaikkoihin Grade Varbi Recruit rekrytointijärjestelmä Evästeet Ehdot Tietosuojakäytäntö Saavutettavuusseloste × Modal title Käytämme evästeitä sisäänkirjautumiseen, käyttökokemuksen parantamiseen, jakolinkkien tarjoamiseen sekä joissakin tapauksissa markkinointiin ja tilastojen keräämiseen. Hyväksy kaikki evästeet Hyväksy vain tarpeelliset Lue lisää evästeistä tässä ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:964775/": {
      "title": "Biostatistician, Lifecourse Medicine, Faculty of Medicine",
      "description": "Biostatistician, Lifecourse Medicine, Faculty of Medicine Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Biostatistician, Lifecourse Medicine, Faculty of Medicine Login and apply Faculty of Medicine, Clinical Medicine The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Biostatistician to join us in the Research Unit of Clinical Medicine for a fixed-term position lasting until 31 December 2029 . You will be based with the Lifecourse Medicine and Birth Cohort Research Group at the Clinical Medicine Research Unit. Our mission in the research group is to understand how exposures early in life, from the fetal period onwards, affect health and well-being during the life course, up to the next generation, and to use this information to advance lifelong health and well-being. We are in particular interested in adult and next-generation outcomes of people born preterm or small for gestational age in high and low resource settings. In our research we use various types of data including whole-population data from national social and healthcare registers from Finland and other Nordic countries and data from clinically studied children and adults in high and low resource settings, including detailed physiological measurements and omics data. About the job As a biostatistician, you will Be responsible for data management including data cleaning, harmonisation and documentation and preparation of analysis datasets of diverse data types such as social and healthcare register data, data from physiological and biochemical measurements, omics data or data collected by wearables. This work is conducted in close connection with other group members, much of it in data secure remote access environments including Findata Kapseli, Statistics Finland Fiona Centre for Scientific Computing CS Desktop or corresponding Nordic environments. The job may include visits to the Nordic and other collaborators' institutions. Contribute to the design of data management solutions to maximise work efficacy and data security. Handle data access and ethics committee applications and other regulatory requirements of use of data. Contribute to research and statistical analysis plans together with other research group members, conduct statistical analyses according to these plans and document their results and methodologies used. Provide advice and take part in training of other group members on data management and data analysis. Take part in other related activities of the research group. Actively train to learn new statistical analysis and data management methods. Depending on the interest and experience of the successful applicant, the job may also include a more active role in developing scientific research questions and writing scientific papers. What we offer Working in one of the globally leading teams studying lifelong outcomes of preterm birth and related traits. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being, and flexible multi-location and remote work opportunities. Read more about other staff benefits. Work-life balance. Development and career options of the big organisation. Work that matters! Read more about working with us. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, excellent education system, and competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu ! Who are you? In order to succeed and enjoy the position, we require from you: A Masters degree in a relevant field including, but not limited to, statistics, mathematics, or bioinformatics. Fluency in written and spoken English Very good familiarity with at least one commonly used statistical software and ability to support and work with group members working with different statistical software. Experience in data management and statistical analysis in research using large quantitative datasets. Good communication and work organisation skills . We also appreciate A doctoral degree. Finnish language skills. The working language of the research group is English, but documentation including that of the data regulatory authorities may be in Finnish. Scientific contributions including scientific publications. The final job description will be shaped according to the skills and interests of the successful candidate. Salary The position is fixed term starting from 1.12.2026 (or as agreed) until 31.12.2029. The salary will be based on the levels MV08-MV09 of the demand level chart for other expert and support staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). Starting gross salary will be approx. 3300-4200 EUR per month (before taxes), depending on experience. A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 1.11.2026 through our recruitment system. Please attach a Cover letter CV Brief description (maximum one page), in your own words, why you apply and how you meet the requirements of this position . The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. Interviews will be held during the latter half of October. The selection process may include more than one interview and a suitability assessment. The shortlisted candidates are also asked to submit their diplomas, and their references will be contacted. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, such as people of different ages, genders, and linguistic, cultural, or minority groups. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact Professor Eero Kajantie, eero.kajantie@oulu.fi , Tel +358 50 473 9438. Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/554 Contact Eero Kajantie, +358504739438, eero.kajantie@oulu.fi Published 23.Sep.2026 Last application date 01.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:972279/": {
      "title": "Biostatistician, Women’s Health Team",
      "description": "Biostatistician, Women’s Health Team Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Biostatistician, Women’s Health Team Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Lääketieteellinen tiedekunta, Kliininen lääketiede Oulun yliopisto on monitieteinen, kansainvälisesti toimiva tiedeyliopisto, jonka noin 4000 työntekijää tuottavat korkeatasoiseen tutkimukseen pohjautuvaa uutta tietoa ja antavat tutkimukseen perustuvaa opetusta kestävämmän, älykkäämmän ja inhimillisemmän maailman rakentamiseksi. Oulun yliopistoyhteisössä toimii kaikkiaan noin 19 000 henkilöä. Pohjoisen tiedeyhteisömme toiminta on globaalisti vaikuttavaa ja luo edellytyksiä innovaatioiden syntymiselle. Kaikkea tutkimus-, opetus- ja työyhteisötoimintaamme ohjaavat yliopistomme arvot sekä eettiset periaatteet. We are now looking for a Biostatistician to join us in Research Unit of Clinical Research for a fixed-term position lasting until 31.12.2027. The Women’s Health Team is a research group at the Faculty of Medicine, University of Oulu. The team advances lifelong gynecological and obstetric health of women and leads internationally recognized programs on women’s health burden and work ability, Polyendocrine Metabolic Ovarian Syndrome (PMOS; formerly PCOS), and hormonal contraception. About the job In this task you work as a statistical expert for the team You use and manage large register data sets (e.g. PMOS-FiRe), cohort data sets (NFBC, WENDY) and questionnaire data sets (FINNETWORK, WeWork). You are involved in all stages of research, from planning to analysis execution, managing data access permits , interpretation, visualization, and publishing Your tasks also include hands-on instruction of students and researchers in statistical analysis, data processing, and variable construction What we offer? The support of an experienced and enthusiastic team of 30 people where you can share your expertise and grow as an expert. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture and well-being and flexible multi-location and remote work opportunities. Read more about other staff benefits here. Work-life balance: we don't count Saturdays as holiday periods! Development and career options of the big organisation. Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and close-ones in settling into Oulu. Work that matters! Read more about working with us. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, excellent education system, and competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu. Who are you? In order to succeed in the position, we expect from you: A University degree in Statistics, Bioinformatics, Mathematics or closely related discipline Experience in statistical data analysis and modelling , as well as data management Fluency in written and spoken English Familiarity with data analysis software (especially R and SPSS, but other options such as SAS or STATA can also be suitable for the role) Ability to work independently and take responsibility for planning and delivering tasks Willingness to learn new methods A genuine interest in women’s health We also appreciate Finnish language skills Knowledge on GDPR regulation in the EU and Finland Experience in register data processing and analysis Familiarity with some of the following: Redcap, CSC environments Experience in bioinformatics is considered a plus, but is not required Your work has an impact on the daily lives of students and researchers at the University of Oulu and will also promote women’s health in general. The final job description will be shaped according to your skills and interests. Salary The position is fixed term starting from 1.12.2026 (or as agreed) until 31.12.2027. The salary will be based on the levels 8-9 of the demand level chart for other expert and support staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary for similar positions typically ranges from approx. 3300-3600 € per month (before taxes). A trial period of 6 months is applied in the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 25.10.2026 through our recruitment system. Please attach an application , CV , and a list of possible publications you have been involved in (describing your role as a statistical expert in each). The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from different backgrounds, such as people of different ages, different genders and members of different language, cultural or minority groups. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact Riikka Arffman, Senior Scientist, riikka.arffman@oulu.fi, +358 503506447 (on weekdays between 9 a.m.- 4 p.m.). Työsuhdemuoto Toistaiseksi Työsuhteen luonne Kokoaikainen Paikkojen lukumäärä 1 Työllisyysaste 100% Paikkakunta Oulu Maakunta Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Maa Suomi Ilmoitusnumero 2026/596 Julkaistu 23.09.2026 Haku päättyy 25.10.2026 Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Jaa linkki Takaisin avoimiin työpaikkoihin Grade Varbi Recruit rekrytointijärjestelmä Evästeet Ehdot Tietosuojakäytäntö Saavutettavuusseloste × Modal title Käytämme evästeitä sisäänkirjautumiseen, käyttökokemuksen parantamiseen, jakolinkkien tarjoamiseen sekä joissakin tapauksissa markkinointiin ja tilastojen keräämiseen. Hyväksy kaikki evästeet Hyväksy vain tarpeelliset Lue lisää evästeistä tässä ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:968327/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher, Ecology and Genetics",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher, Ecology and Genetics Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral Researcher, Ecology and Genetics Login and apply Faculty of Science, Ecology and Genetics The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Postdoctoral Researcher to join us, Global Change and Biotic Interactions Ecology -group, for the Research Council of Finland-funded project “ Mechanisms of Plant Biodiversity Change ”, both led by Prof. Anu Eskelinen ( Eskelinen Research Group | Global Change and Biotic Interaction Ecology ). Description of the position We are looking for a highly motivated and talented, strongly research-oriented person to carry out postdoctoral research addressing the mechanisms of plant biodiversity change. In this project, we investigate what are the roles of mechanisms related to spatial context, dispersal in space and time, biotic interactions (competition, herbivory) and intraspecific trait change in driving heterogeneous responses of plant biodiversity to different global change factors (e.g., climate warming, nutrient enrichment). We aim for a more holistic understanding of plant biodiversity change in the Anthropocene, being able to provide answers to questions: how, why and where plant biodiversity changes. The research questions can relate, for example, to (1) the role of seed banks as a diversity maintaining mechanism under multiple global changes, (2) the role of competition for light and other mechanisms such as litter and loss of herbivory in driving diversity loss under climatic and other global changes, and (3) the role of intraspecific trait change in modifying the effects of climatic and other global changes on plant biodiversity. These will be developed together with the project leader. The postdoctoral researcher in collaboration with the project leader and collaborators will use existing data from long-term global change experiments, analyze data, and write manuscripts/publish articles in highly reputable international journals. These data come from two experiments: (1) eDiValo experiment that was designed to test the ecological impacts of light on plant community diversity (Eskelinen et al. 2022 Nature), and (2) a long-term experiment in tundra manipulating temperature, grazing and nutrients (Kaarlejärvi et al. 2017 Nat Comm). There is also a possibility for some experimental field work, although the position is mostly targeted using already existing long-term experimental data. Other duties may include teaching in undergraduate/graduate courses and co-supervising master's and doctoral students and contributing to developing new proposals to continue further research in this area. In addition, you may have to participate in administrative tasks of the university and/or the Ecology and Genetics Unit. Although the position will be based at the Ecology and Genetics Research Unit in Oulu, the doctoral researcher will also collaborate with an international researcher team from, for example, the University of Utrecht, Netherlands, the German Centre for Integrative Biodiversity Research iDiv, Germany, and the University of Helsinki, Finland. There may also be research visit(s) to these collabortors’ groups. We also expect participation to international conferences. Qualification requirements for the Postdoctoral researcher position PhD in plant community ecology or equivalent field (obtained within the past 10 years) Demonstrated ability to prepare independently high-impact manuscripts/publications for international journals Demonstrated experience and knowledge of plant biodiversity research, experimental research, global change research, trait-based plant ecology, or some combination of these Strong statistical, data exploration and data management skills, excellent skills with software R Knowledge of grassland ecosystems (e.g., temperate, tundra) Ability for independent scientific work Open-mindedness, curiosity, strong motivation and enthusiasm towards research and science Excellent written and spoken English Good communication and teamwork skills. Assessment of the applicants will be based on, acknowledging the content of the job, 1) overall fit to the above profile, 2) scientific publications, 3) motivation, 4) previous work experience, 5) national and international mobility and networking skills, and 5) other academic activities and merits. What we offer You will become a part of a highly enthusiastic and talented research group that is working on globally significant research areas The support of an experienced and enthusiastic research team where you can share and grow your expertise. Inspiring, novel, and ambitious study questions/systems Possibility for a flexible combination of presence work and remote work (this can be negotiated, depending on the situation of the applicant and project demands) Full benefits provided by the University of Oulu to university employees, including free time corresponding to holidays and free occupational health care services. The successful candidate will also receive benefits provided by the Finnish government to residents, for example, the possibility to obtain access to the national healthcare system, tax benefits for employees with children, and high-quality affordable childcare services. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits here. Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. We have an HR Excellence in Research quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety,an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu. Salary The position is fixed-term for two (2) years as of February 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. The start date is flexible and can be negotiated. The salary will be based on the levels 5-6 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary will be approx. 3900-4300 € per month (before taxes). A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by November 15 , 2026 (23:59 Finnish local time, UTC +3) through our recruitment system. Only applications sent via the online system will be considered. The application should be written in English and include the following: A motivation letter (max. 2 pages) summarizing the applicant’s professional experience, expertise, research interests and motivation, and describing why the applicant is interested in this position. Also, information on personal career plans are highly encouraged. CV , following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity List of publications , following the guidelines of the Research Council of Finland Contact information of two senior/experienced researcher s who may be asked to give a statement on the candidate The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on- site or remote interview. The shortlisted candidates will also be asked to submit their diplomas, and their references will be contacted. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Contact Information For further information, please contact Professor Anu Eskelinen (anu.eskelinen(at)oulu.fi) Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Salary TES Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/568 Published 24.Sep.2026 Last application date 15.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:968629/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher, Ecology and Genetics",
      "description": "Doctoral Researcher, Ecology and Genetics Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral Researcher, Ecology and Genetics Login and apply Faculty of Science, Ecology and Genetics The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Doctoral Researcher to join us, Global Change and Biotic Interactions Ecology -group, for the Research Council of Finland-funded project “ Mechanisms of Plant Biodiversity Change ”, both led by Prof. Anu Eskelinen ( Eskelinen Research Group | Global Change and Biotic Interaction Ecology ). Description of the project We are looking for a highly motivated and research-oriented person to carry out doctoral research addressing the mechanisms of plant biodiversity change. In this project, we investigate what are the roles of mechanisms related to spatial context, dispersal in space and time, biotic interactions (competition, herbivory) and intraspecific trait change in driving heterogeneous responses of plant biodiversity to different global change factors (e.g., climate warming, nutrient enrichment). We aim for a more holistic understanding of plant biodiversity change in the Anthropocene, being able to provide answers to questions: how, why and where plant biodiversity changes. The specific research questions can relate, for example, to (1) the role of temporal dispersal via soil seed banks as a diversity maintaining mechanism under multiple global changes, (2) the role of intraspecific trait change in modifying the effects of climatic and other global changes on plant biodiversity, and (3) relative and interactive roles of spatial context (i.e., connectivity and habitat size), dispersal and herbivory in mediating plant biodiversity response to global changes. A suitable combination of these questions/ideas will be developed together with the project leader. We use already existing data (ready to be analyzed) and will also collect new data from two unique, existing long-term experimental systems to address these research questions. Your tasks As a Doctoral Researcher, you will conduct research in the “Mechanisms of Plant Biodiversity Change” project described above and complete a doctoral degree and studies studies at the University of Oulu Graduate School. Your specific tasks are: Collecting new data on plant communities (field, greenhouse and laboratory work), including organizing and planning the work Conducting plant trait measurements Conducting statistical analyses on new and already existing research data from long-term field experiments Writing manuscripts (2-3) and publishing the research findings in high-quality international peer-reviewed journals under the guidance/supervision of your mentor and in collaboration with other researchers Participating national and international conferences and workshops, when relevant Teaching in BSc/MSc level courses and co-supervising master's students and interns. Being an active member of the working group Although the position will be based at the Ecology and Genetics Research Unit in Oulu, the doctoral researcher will also collaborate with an international researcher team from, for example, the University of Helsinki, Finland and the University of California, Davis, USA. There may also be research visit(s) to these collabortors’ groups. Qualification requirements for the Doctoral researcher position MSc in plant community ecology or equivalent field Strong motivation, curiosity, and enthusiasm towards ecological research and to pursue doctoral studies Experience and interest in some of the following: plant biodiversity research, experimental research, global change research, trait-based plant ecology Excellent statistical skills with software R Ability to travel and do field work, experience in field work Good grassland plant identification skills and ability to quickly learn new species Knowledge of grassland ecosystems (e.g., temperate, tundra) Excellent written and spoken English Good communication and teamwork skills, ability to work in an international team Driver’s licence is needed or willingness to acquire one See also the requirements of the University of Oulu Graduate School (UniOGS) Assessment of the applicants will be based on, acknowledging the content of the job, 1) overall fit to the above profile, 2) scientific publications (if applicable), 3) motivation, 4) previous work experience, 5) national and international mobility and networking skills, and 5) other academic activities and merits. What we offer A three-year, full-time Doctoral Researcher position in an ambitious project Opportunities for national and international collaboration, conference participation, co- authored publications and research mobility if relevant to your doctoral project You will become a part of a highly enthusiastic and talented research group that is working on globally significant research areas Possibility for a flexible combination of presence work and remote work (this can be negotiated, depending on the situation of the applicant and project demands) Full benefits provided by the University of Oulu to university employees, including free time corresponding to holidays and free occupational health care services. The successful candidate will receive also benefits provided by the Finnish government to residents, for example possibility to obtain access to the national healthcare system, tax benefits for employees with children, and high-quality affordable childcare services. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits here. Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu. Salary The position is fixed-term for three (3) years as of February 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. The start date is flexible and can be negotiated. The salary will be based on the levels 2-4 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The typical starting gross salary will be approx. 2600-3000 € per month (before taxes). As the doctoral research progresses, there is salary progression in accordance with the University salary system. A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by November 15, 2026 (23:59 Finnish local time, UTC +3) through our recruitment system. Only applications sent via the online system will be considered. The application should be written in English and include the following: 1. A motivation letter (max. 2 pages) summarizing the applicant’s professional experience, and expertise, research interests and motivation, and describing why the applicant is interested in this position. The motivation letter should also include contact information of two senior/experienced researchers who may be asked to give a statement on the shortlisted candidates. 2. CV , following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity 3. List of publications , if applicable, following the guidelines of the Research Council of Finland 4. A copy of the relevant degree certificate or diploma ; if the qualifying degree is not yet complete, please describe your expected completion date The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on- site or remote interview. The refernces of the shortlisted candidates will also contacted. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Contact Information For further information, please contact Professor Anu Eskelinen (anu.eskelinen(at)oulu.fi) Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Salary TES Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/572 Published 24.Sep.2026 Last application date 15.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:970235/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher, Space Physics, Faculty of Science",
      "description": "Doctoral Researcher, Space Physics, Faculty of Science Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral Researcher, Space Physics, Faculty of Science Login and apply Faculty of Science, Space Physics and Astronomy The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Doctoral Researcher for a maximum of four years, starting at the earliest on 1st of January 2027 to work in a Research Council of Finland project Space climate of cosmic ray anisotropies - SOCRATES, led by Dr. Pauli Väisänen, in collaboration with the other researchers of the Space Physics and Astronomy Research Unit (SPA RU) at the Faculty of Science. The SPA RU includes research groups in Ionospheric Physics, Space Climate, Cosmic Rays, and Astronomy. The unit is a part of the Finnish Centre of Excellence and is involved in several large-scale research projects. It is involved in top-level research, both experimental and theoretical, in the fields of heliospheric, magnetospheric, and ionospheric physics, cosmic rays and atmospheric effects, and planetary sciences. This position is open in the Cosmic Rays research group led by Professor Ilya Usoskin. The successful applicant will work in a compact, active, dynamic, and highly international research group. About the job The Space climate of cosmic ray anisotropies - SOCRATES project aims to detect low-amplitude cosmic ray anisotropies using neutron monitor and other near-Earth space and ground level observations. The ultimate goal is to analyse these anisotropies to perform tomography of different heliospheric directions and regions affected by solar activity and the space climate. The succesful applicant will perform modeling of the measured cosmic ray fluxes and backtrace them to different heliospheric directions. Your tasks in the project will include: You will be an active member of a top-level multidisciplinary research group You will perform modeling of cosmic ray flux variation, the predicted arrival directions and particle movements in the magnetosphere & heliosphere. This is done with high-resolution cosmic ray and other data, for with collection and validation across many instruments and datasets will be performed. You will closely collaborate with the SOCRATES project PI and the wider research group working on space climate, solar-terrestrial and cosmic ray physics. You are expected to write and publish scientific peer-reviewed articles in high-level journals and present the results at scientific conferences. You will perform necessary graduate studies and complete and successfully defend a doctoral thesis on a topic related to the SOCRATES project at the end of the period. What we offer The support of an experienced and enthusiastic team of about 40 people, with whom you can share your expertise and grow as an expert. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits. Development and career options of the big organization. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us . Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu. Who are you? In order to succeed and enjoy the position, we require from you: A completed M.Sc. degree or equivalent in Space Physics, Geosciences, Astroparticle Physics, or another field directly relevant to the project is required before the start of the employment. Ability to work independently and in a team, including scientific writing. Good command of written and spoken English. You must apply for the right to study for a doctoral degree at the beginning of your employment in accordance with the requirements of the University of Oulu Graduate School (UniOGS). We also appreciate Knowledge of physics related to solar & heliospheric physics, geosciences, electrodynamics and magnetohydrodynamics. Understanding and know-how of the measurements of neutron monitors, other cosmic ray detectors and heliospheric and near-Earth in-situ spacecraft detectors. Experience in numerical modelling, knowledge of programming languages (e.g., Python, Matlab, C) Ability and willingness to learn new things. Good communication skills. See also the requirements of the University of Oulu Graduate School (UniOGS). Salary The position is fixed-term for 4 years as of 1.1.2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. A 6 month trial period will be applied to the position. The work will be performed in person in the  Linnanmaa campus of the University of Oulu. The salary will be based on the levels 2-4 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary will be approx. 2600-3200 € per month (before taxes). How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 11.10.2026 (23:59 Finnish local time) through our recruitment system. The application should be written in English and include the following: Cover letter (max 2 pages), including a description of your experience and motivations related to the position CV (max 3 pages) following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity List of publications (if any), following the guidelines of the Academy of Finland. The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact Academy Research Fellow Pauli Väisänen (e-mail: pauli.vaisanen at oulu.fi) Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Employment expires 2030-12-31 Contract type Full time First day of employment 1.1.2027 Salary TES Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/582 Contact Pauli Väisänen, Academy Research Fellow, pauli.vaisanen@oulu.fi Published 24.Sep.2026 Last application date 11.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:965554/": {
      "title": "Senior Research Fellow in Ethics in Artificial Intelligence",
      "description": "Senior Research Fellow in Ethics in Artificial Intelligence Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Senior Research Fellow in Ethics in Artificial Intelligence Login and apply Multidisciplinary recruitment The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Senior Research Fellow in Ethics in Artificial Intelligence for a two-year fixed-term position to contribute to Hybrid Intelligence research program.  The position will be based in one of the following faculties, or possibly jointly across several faculties depending on the expertise level: the Faculty of Education and Psychology, the Faculty of Information Technology and Electrical Engineering, and/or the Faculty of Medicine. About the job The successful candidate will be expected to conduct advanced research in ethics, with a particular focus on AI ethics and to work collaboratively with researchers across disciplines within the Hybrid Intelligence (HI) research community. One of the key responsibilities is to lead the Ethics Forum. The Ethics Forum facilitates new research and discussion on the transdisciplinary ethical, value-related, and societal dimensions of Hybrid Intelligence. In addition, the successful candidate will be expected to provide research-led teaching and supervise postgraduate research. What we offer We offer you a supportive academic environment in a community of committed Hybrid Intelligence scholars and the possibility to use funding opportunities to generate new research ideas and build an innovative program that will attract international scholars. The University of Oulu offers flexible working hours, an excellent work-life balance, and a range of occupational healthcare services. Our competitive salaries include paid leave and an additional holiday bonus in the summer. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy.  Oulu is known for its beautiful natural surroundings, vibrant cultural life, and friendly, easy-going atmosphere. Residents enjoy Finland’s high standard of living together with relatively affordable housing. Read more about living in Oulu . We also offer Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits here. Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. Development and career options of the big organization. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us. Who are you? When assessing the candidate’s merits for the position, attention will be paid to scientific excellence, such as research outputs, international scientific activities and collaboration, supervision of undergraduate students, pedagogical competence, societal relevance, impact and potential of scientific activities, and services for the academic community. To succeed and enjoy the position, we expect you to have: A doctoral degree in a relevant field and a strong research track record in AI ethics Demonstrated scientific research experience and relevant teaching skills The ability to lead research and experience in acquiring external research funding Relevant experience in international scientific work and collaboration Experience in research that integrates perspectives and methods across disciplines. Excellent written and interpersonal communication skills Salary The position is fixed-term for two year as of 16.11.2026 or as soon as possible thereafter. The salary will be based on the levels 6-7 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary will be approx. 4400-5500 € per month (before taxes). A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 11.10.2026 (23:59 Finnish local time) through our recruitment system. The application should be written in English and include the following: Cover letter CV , following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity List of publications , following the guidelines of the Research Council of Finland Brief account of research merits (max. 2 pages) Teaching Portfolio , following the guidelines of the University of Oulu Details regarding the acquisition of research funds A brief research and action plan relating to Hybrid Intelligence ethics (max 2 p.) Contact information of 2–4 persons available for recommendation The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. The shortlisted candidates will also be asked to submit their diplomas, and their references will be contacted. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact the coordinator of Hybrid Intelligence research program Dr. Satu Kaleva; satu.kaleva(at)oulu.fi. Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/559 Contact Satu Kaleva, +358504787744, satu.kaleva@oulu.fi Sanna Järvelä, sanna.jarvela@oulu.fi Published 25.Sep.2026 Last application date 11.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:972258/": {
      "title": "Yliopistoharjoittelija (viestintä)",
      "description": "Yliopistoharjoittelija (viestintä) Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Yliopistoharjoittelija (viestintä) Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Palvelu- ja erillisyksiköt, Innovaatiokeskus Oulun yliopisto on monitieteinen, kansainvälisesti toimiva tiedeyliopisto, jonka noin 4000 työntekijää tuottavat korkeatasoiseen tutkimukseen pohjautuvaa uutta tietoa ja antavat tutkimukseen perustuvaa opetusta kestävämmän, älykkäämmän ja inhimillisemmän maailman rakentamiseksi. Oulun yliopistoyhteisössä toimii kaikkiaan noin 19 000 henkilöä. Pohjoisen tiedeyhteisömme toiminta on globaalisti vaikuttavaa ja luo edellytyksiä innovaatioiden syntymiselle. Kaikkea tutkimus-, opetus- ja työyhteisötoimintaamme ohjaavat yliopistomme arvot sekä eettiset periaatteet. Haemme nyt Oulun yliopiston Innovaatiokeskukseen Yliopistoharjoittelijaa määräaikaiseen 3-6 kk työsuhteeseen. Innovaatiokeskuksessa a utamme tutkijoita tutkimustulosten kaupallistamiseen ja immateriaalioikeuksiin liittyvissä kysymyksissä, liiketoimintapotentiaalin löytämisessä ja liikeideoiden kehittämisessä, Business Finlandin tutkimusrahoitusten hakemisessa ja yhteistyöverkoston rakentamisessa yrityselämän kanssa. Autamme myös yrittäjähenkisiä opiskelijoita eteenpäin sekä edistämme yhteistyötä opiskelijoiden ja yritysten välillä. Seuraa meitä ja lue lisää LinkedInissä , Instagramissa ja InnoBlogissa ! Etsimme yliopistoharjoittelijaa luomaan sisältöjä tutkimuksesta, innovaatioista, yrittäjyydestä ja yritysyhteistyöstä. Hae meille kehittämään osaamistasi käytännössä asiantuntevan tiimin tuella! Työtehtävät Yliopistoharjoittelijana osallistut esimerkiksi: uutisten, artikkelien ja uutiskirjeiden kirjoittamiseen sisällöntuotantoon sosiaalisen median kanavissa tapahtumien sekä tapahtumaviestinnän suunnitteluun ja toteutukseen verkkosivujen sisältöjen tuottamiseen ja päivittämiseen viestinnän ja markkinoinnin muihin käytännön tehtäviin. Mitä tarjoamme? Tuen asiantuntevalta ja innostuneelta 15 hengen tiimiltä, jossa pääset kehittymään ja jakamaan asiantuntemustasi. Työn ja vapaa-ajan tasapainoa sekä joustavat monipaikka- ja etätyömahdollisuudet. Ison organisaation tarjoamat kehitys- ja uramahdollisuudet. Merkityksellisen työn! Lisätietoa työskentelystä Oulun yliopistossa . Harjoittelusta Innovaatiokeskuksella saat: monipuolista käytännön kokemusta viestinnästä ja markkinoinnista mahdollisuuden tutustua tutkimuksen kaupallistamiseen, innovaatioihin, yrittäjyyteen ja yritysyhteistyöhön sisältöjä ja työnäytteitä oman osaamisesi tueksi asiantuntevaa ohjausta ja palautetta joustavan ja kannustavan työympäristön mahdollisuuden verkostoitua tutkijoiden, opiskelijoiden ja yhteistyökumppaneiden kanssa. Mitä etsimme? Onnistuaksesi ja viihtyäksesi tehtävässä edellytämme sinulta: soveltuvia korkeakouluopintoja esimerkiksi viestinnän, markkinoinnin, suomen kielen tai kauppatieteiden parissa; harjoittelun tulee olla osa korkeakouluopintojasi (opintopisteet) hyvää suomen ja englannin kielen kirjallista ja suullista taitoa kiinnostusta kirjoittamiseen, sisällöntuotantoon ja digitaaliseen viestintään valmiutta työskennellä sekä itsenäisesti että yhdessä muiden kanssa. Eduksi katsomme kokemuksen: sosiaalisen median (esim. LinkedIn, Instagram) sisällöntuotannosta kuvien, videoiden tai muiden visuaalisten sisältöjen tekemisestä Canvan tai muiden viestinnän työkalujen käytöstä. Sinun ei kuitenkaan tarvitse osata kaikkea valmiiksi. Arvostamme uteliaisuutta ja halua oppia. Tehtävän palkkaus Tehtävä on määräaikainen 23.11.2026 alkaen (tai sopimuksen mukaan) ja kestää 3-6 kuukautta tilanteestasi riippuen. Toivomme, että pystyt aloittamaan harjoittelun jo marras-joulukuussa 2026. Tarkempi aloitusajankohta voidaan sopia tilanteesi ja tiimimme aikataulujen mukaan. Harjoittelun palkka on 1736,41 e/kk. Tehtävässä sovelletaan koeaikaa, joka on enintään puolet työsuhteen kestosta. Yliopistoharjoittelija saa kaksi lomapäivää täydeltä lomanmääräytymiskuukaudelta. Ansaitut lomapäivät tulee pitää harjoitteluajan sisällä. Kuinka hakea? Jos kiinnostuit, lähetäthän hakemuksesi (maksimipituus 1 sivu) ja CV:si rekrytointijärjestelmän kautta viimeistään 18.10.2026. Kerro hakemuksessasi lyhyesti: miksi tehtävä kiinnostaa sinua? millaista viestintäosaamista sinulla on? millaisia sisältöjä olet aiemmin tuottanut? mitä haluaisit oppia harjoittelun aikana? Voit liittää mukaan myös työnäytteitä tai linkkejä tekemiisi sisältöihin. Tehtävään parhaiten soveltuvat hakijat kutsutaan haastatteluun etäyhteydellä tai kasvokkain. Tulemme olemaan yhteydessä kaikkiin hakijoihin hakuprosessin aikana. Lisätietoja Jäikö jokin arveluttamaan? Ota yhteyttä: Niina Pakonen, v iestinnän ja markkinoinnin suunnittelija , Oulun yliopiston Innovaatiokeskus , niina.pakonen(at)oulu.fi , +358 50 475 4621 Työsuhdemuoto Määräaikainen 3-6 kuukautta Työsuhteen luonne Kokoaikainen Palkka 1736,41 e/kk Paikkojen lukumäärä 1 Työllisyysaste 100% Paikkakunta Oulu Maakunta Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Maa Suomi Ilmoitusnumero 2026/595 Yhteys Niina Pakonen, +358504754621, niina.pakonen@oulu.fi Julkaistu 28.09.2026 Haku päättyy 18.10.2026 Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Jaa linkki Takaisin avoimiin työpaikkoihin Grade Varbi Recruit rekrytointijärjestelmä Evästeet Ehdot Tietosuojakäytäntö Saavutettavuusseloste × Modal title Käytämme evästeitä sisäänkirjautumiseen, käyttökokemuksen parantamiseen, jakolinkkien tarjoamiseen sekä joissakin tapauksissa markkinointiin ja tilastojen keräämiseen. Hyväksy kaikki evästeet Hyväksy vain tarpeelliset Lue lisää evästeistä tässä ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:969731/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher, Faculty of Education and Psychology, Learning and Learning Process",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher, Faculty of Education and Psychology, Learning and Learning Process Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral Researcher, Faculty of Education and Psychology, Learning and Learning Process Login and apply Faculty of Education and Psychology, Learning and Learning Process The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Postdoctoral Researcher to join us in the Learning and Educational Technology research Lab (LET Lab) at the Faculty of Educational and Psychology About the job In this position, you will contribute to research within the Learning and Educational Technology (LET) Lab, focusing on the design and evaluation of AI-supported technologies that promote regulation of learning in collaborative contexts. The research integrates learning sciences, human-computer interaction, software development, and human-AI collaboration to better understand and support learning processes in authentic educational settings. You will lead the technical development and evaluation of evidence-based technologies that support regulation of learning in collaboration, and human-AI complementarity in education. The position is situated within a broader research portfolio focused on self- and socially shared regulation in learning, the role of teachers, and technology-enhanced learning across K-12, higher education, and emerging learning environments. You will conduct research within a team, manage project-related tasks, and disseminate research findings in leading international conferences and scientific journals. The topic will be closely connected to the Hybrid Intelligence research programme in Oulu University. What we offer? Globally recognized researchers within the LET Lab, connected to an extensive international network through the University of Oulu’s Hybrid Intelligence Research Programme, partner institutions, and collaborators across Europe. The support of an experienced and enthusiastic team of people where you can share your expertise and grow as an expert. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits . Development and career options of the big organization. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us. We have a HR Excellence in Research -quality label which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, excellent education system, and competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu . Who are you? In order to succeed and enjoy the position, we expect from you: Doctoral degree in human-computer interaction, computer sciences, digital design, interaction design, edtech design, learning sciences or related areas. The degree must be obtained no more than 10 years ago A good understanding of learning theories, such as self-regulated learning theory, or a strong interest in learning about them. Experience in research data collection, qualitative data coding, and analysis. Experience with theory-drive quantitative data analysis (R/SPSS, Python). Software development (Python), experience using cloud-based high-performance computing systems; experience with specialist software (Praat, NVivo, Observer) is a plus but not required. Interest in human-AI complementarity, including prior experience with topics such as human-computer interaction, real-time spoken natural language processing, legal and ethical considerations in processing sensitive data. Fluent spoken and written English, knowledge of Finnish is a plus. Agentic work approach and good collaboration and academic writing skills. Ability to engage in independent scientific research or artistic work Teaching competence required for the position About the job As a postdoctoral researcher, you will engage in innovative research within learning sciences leveraging your own particular expertise. In the project, your responsibilities will include: gaining deep understanding of an existing agent architecture designed for supporting regulation in collaborative learning (backend, speech processing pipeline, data flow) identifying what can be reused or needs to be rebuilt for a Python-based implementation and if needed, creating a concrete workplan for the implementation of the agent architecture in Python evaluating and advising the research team on future infrastructure options (e.g. server-based vs local or edge deployment) to fit evolving project needs translating research and usability needs (e.g. ease of use for non-technical researchers, reliability across data collection sessions) into concrete technical decisions ensuring clear documentation of the system design and implementation choices is maintained for a non-technical audience collaborating with the research team to align technical development with the conceptual development of the agent and study goals contributing to the design of the agent by translating socially shared regulation of learning theory into innovative design solutions and functionalities designing and conducting laboratory and in-situ studies to evaluate and refine the agent analyzing multimodal data (e.g. video, physiological signals) for assessing the agent’s impact on learning processes publishing your findings in high-impact journals and presenting work at relevant conferences. As a member of the Learning and Educational Technology research lab, you will collaborate with a multidisciplinary research group, contributing to joint publications and other research efforts. Additionally, you will have the opportunity to mentor junior researchers and participate in international conferences and workshops. Salary The position is fixed-term starting 15.11.2026 or as soon as possible thereafter, until 30.6.2028. The salary will be based on the levels 5-6 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). Starting gross salary will be approx. 3600-4200 € per month (before taxes). A trial period of 6 months is applied in the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 25.10.2026 ( 23:59 Finnish local time) through our recruitment system. The application should be written in English and include the following: CV , following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity Cover letter List of publications , following the guidelines of the Academy of Finland Certificates/Diplomas Contact information of 2 persons available for recommendation The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, such as people of different ages, different genders and members of different language, cultural or minority groups. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact: Sanna.jarvela@oulu.fi Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/579 Contact Sanna Marketta Järvelä, sanna.jarvela@oulu.fi Published 05.Oct.2026 Last application date 25.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:972502/": {
      "title": "Yliopistoharjoittelija, Kansainvälisen liikkuvuuden palvelut",
      "description": "Yliopistoharjoittelija, Kansainvälisen liikkuvuuden palvelut Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Yliopistoharjoittelija, Kansainvälisen liikkuvuuden palvelut Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Palvelu- ja erillisyksiköt, Koulutuspalvelut Oulun yliopisto on monitieteinen, kansainvälisesti toimiva tiedeyliopisto, jonka noin 4000 työntekijää tuottavat korkeatasoiseen tutkimukseen pohjautuvaa uutta tietoa ja antavat tutkimukseen perustuvaa opetusta kestävämmän, älykkäämmän ja inhimillisemmän maailman rakentamiseksi. Oulun yliopistoyhteisössä toimii kaikkiaan noin 19 000 henkilöä. Pohjoisen tiedeyhteisömme toiminta on globaalisti vaikuttavaa ja luo edellytyksiä innovaatioiden syntymiselle. Kaikkea tutkimus-, opetus- ja työyhteisötoimintaamme ohjaavat yliopistomme arvot sekä eettiset periaatteet. Etsimme nyt Oulun yliopiston Koulutuspalveluihin, Kansainvälisen liikkuvuuden palveluiden tiimiin Yliopistoharjoittelijaa osa-aikaiseen (75 %, eli noin 27 tuntia viikossa), määräaikaiseen työsuhteeseen 1.1.-30.4.2027. Työtehtävät Yliopistoharjoittelijana autat saapuvien ja lähtevien vaihto-opiskelijoiden palveluissa, esimerkiksi osallistumalla tapahtumien järjestelyihin ja toteutukseen tiimin tukena sekä suunnittelemalla ja laatimalla materiaaleja. Markkinointitehtäviisi kuuluu vaihtolähettilästoiminnan tukeminen, kansainvälisen liikkuvuuden palveluiden esittely sosiaalisessa mediassa sekä vaihtohakuihin liittyvissä markkinointikampanjoissa avustaminen. Tehtäviisi kuuluu liikkuvuusjärjestelmän tietojen sisällöllisistä käsittelyä, kuten vaihtokohde- ja kumppaniyliopistotietojen päivittämistä, vaihtopalautteiden käsittelyä ja analysointia sekä tietojen tarkistamista ja anonymisointia. Harjoitteluusi voi kuulua myös muita kansainväliseen liikkuvuuteen liittyviä avustavia tehtäviä. Voit myös itse esittää toiveita siitä mihin haluaisit perehtyä. Tehtävä sijoittuu Linnanmaan kampukselle. Mitä tarjoamme? Tuen asiantuntevalta ja innostuneelta tiimiltä, jossa pääset kehittymään ja jakamaan asiantuntemustasi. Ison organisaation tarjoamat kehitys- ja uramahdollisuudet. Merkityksellisen työn! Lisätietoa työskentelystä Oulun yliopistossa . Mitä etsimme? Onnistuaksesi ja viihtyäksesi tehtävässä edellytämme sinulta: Olet suorittanut korkeakouluopintoja vähintään vuoden ajan. Koulutusalasi voi olla mikä tahansa. Harjoittelun täytyy kuulua osaksi opintojasi (opintopisteet). Hyvää yleiskäsitystä korkeakoulutuksesta, opiskelijan kansainvälistymismahdollisuuksista ja Oulun yliopistosta Erinomaisia viestintä- ja ICT-taitoja, reipasta palveluasennetta, tarkkuutta sekä kykyä työskennellä itsenäisesti ja aloitteellisesti Erinomaista suomen ja englannin kielen taitoa Eduksi katsomme: Muu kielitaito Omakohtainen kansainvälinen kokemus Tehtävän palkkaus Tehtävä on osa-aikainen, määräaikainen 1.1.2027 alkaen ja päättyy 30.4.2027. Osa-aikaisen (75 %, eli noin 27 tuntia viikossa) yliopistoharjoittelijan palkka on 1302,31 e/kk. Tehtävässä sovelletaan koeaikaa, joka on enintään puolet työsuhteen kestosta. Yliopistoharjoittelija saa kaksi lomapäivää täydeltä lomanmääräytymiskuukaudelta. Ansaitut lomapäivät tulee pitää harjoitteluajan sisällä. Kuinka hakea? Jos kiinnostuit, lähetäthän hakemuksen rekrytointijärjestelmän kautta viimeistään 25.10.2026 . Liitä mukaan hakemuskirje ja CV. Tehtävään parhaiten soveltuvat hakijat kutsutaan haastatteluun. Haastattelut pidetään 2.-9.11.2026. Tulemme olemaan yhteydessä kaikkiin hakijoihin hakuprosessin aikana. Lisätietoja Jäikö jokin arveluttamaan? Ota yhteyttä: Kehittämispäällikkö Marianne Isola (marianne.isola(at)oulu.fi, +358504087990), tavoitettavissa parhaiten 12.10. klo 9-12 ja 14.10. klo 13-16. Työsuhdemuoto Määräaikainen 3-6 kuukautta Työsopimus päättyy 2027-04-30 Työsuhteen luonne Osa-aikainen Työsuhteen toivottu aloitusajankohta 1.1.2027 Palkka 1302,31 e/kk Paikkojen lukumäärä 1 Työllisyysaste 75 % Paikkakunta Oulu Maakunta Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Maa Suomi Ilmoitusnumero 2026/597 Yhteys Marianne Isola, +358504087990, marianne.isola@oulu.fi Julkaistu 05.10.2026 Haku päättyy 25.10.2026 Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Jaa linkki Takaisin avoimiin työpaikkoihin Grade Varbi Recruit rekrytointijärjestelmä Evästeet Ehdot Tietosuojakäytäntö Saavutettavuusseloste × Modal title Käytämme evästeitä sisäänkirjautumiseen, käyttökokemuksen parantamiseen, jakolinkkien tarjoamiseen sekä joissakin tapauksissa markkinointiin ja tilastojen keräämiseen. Hyväksy kaikki evästeet Hyväksy vain tarpeelliset Lue lisää evästeistä tässä ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:951038/": {
      "title": "(Postdoctoral) Project Researcher, Ecology and Genetics",
      "description": "(Postdoctoral) Project Researcher, Ecology and Genetics Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) (Postdoctoral) Project Researcher, Ecology and Genetics Login and apply Faculty of Science, Ecology and Genetics The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for Project Researcher with a Doctoral Degree to join our Stream Ecology Research Group in the ecology and genetics research unit for a fixed-term position lasting until 31.10.2027 to work on themes related to stream community responses to changes in climate, hydrology, land use and nutrient availability in sub-arctic and arctic areas. About the job The position is linked to the “ Greener rivers in the warming Arctic? Anticipating the short- and long-term effects of additional nutrient inputs ” research project funded by the Research Council of Finland ( Greener rivers in the warming Arctic? Anticipating the short- and long-term effects of additional nutrient inputs. - Research.fi ) and the university's \"Safeguarding biodiversity through interdisciplinary research on habitat restoration\" profiling programme ( Safeguarding biodiversity through interdisciplinary research on habitat restoration (SAFIRE) | University of Oulu) . In our research we use field observations, mesocosm and field experiments and existing monitoring data on biotic communities at different temporal and spatial scales coupled with environmental data from various sources. Our key interests lie at the bottom of the food webs: the diversity of benthic microbes and invertebrates and the rates of associated ecological functions in relation to environmental change. Work tasks include all steps of research. Thus you are expected to participate in planning and conducting research analyzing research data writing scientific papers communicating research results The position may include field work mainly in Northern Finland. A successful candidate is also expected to contribute to some degree to teaching and / or supervision of both doctoral and undergraduate students. What we offer The support of an enthusiastic research team and networks, where you can share your expertise and grow as an expert. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being, and flexible multi-location and remote work opportunities. Read more about other staff benefits. Work-life balance: we don't count Saturdays as holiday periods! Development and career options of the big organisation. Work that matters! Read more about working with us. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, excellent education system, and competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu ! Who are you? You should hold a recent PhD degree (no more than five years; or you will obtain the degree by the end of 2026) for example in ecology or physical geography with peer-reviewed publications in high-standard international journals. You should also possess a firm understanding of the principles of research design and advanced skills in statistical analyses, preferably using R. Experience on climate and land use change research is considered beneficial. Proficiency in English is essential. As personal qualities we appreciate: cooperation and communication skills ability to work both independently and as a team member enthusiasm, creativity and innovative approach active participation in the research group and networks Salary The position is fixed-term starting from 01.11.2026 (or as agreed) until 31.10.2027. The salary will be based on the level MV9 of the demand level chart for other expert and support staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). Starting gross salary will be approx. 3900 - 4000 EUR per month (before taxes) for a person with a doctoral degree. A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 22.10.2026 through our recruitment system. Please attach a motivation letter (max 2 pages) and CV including the list of your key publications. Note, the interviews of potential candidates may begin already when the call is open. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact assistant professor Kaisa-Leena Huttunen, kaisa-leena.huttunen@oulu.fi. Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Employment expires 2027-10-31 Contract type Full time First day of employment 1.11.2026 Salary TES Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/470 Contact Kaisa-Leena Huttunen, kaisa-leena.huttunen@oulu.fi Published 08.Oct.2026 Last application date 22.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:973985/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher, Human-AI Shared Regulation of Learning",
      "description": "Doctoral Researcher, Human-AI Shared Regulation of Learning Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral Researcher, Human-AI Shared Regulation of Learning Login and apply Faculty of Education and Psychology, Learning and Learning Processes (LLP) The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for 1-2 candidates for the position of Doctoral Researcher to join us in the  Learning and Educational Technology (LET) Lab, within the Learning and Learning Processes (LLP) Research Unit at the Faculty of Education and Psychology The Learning and Educational Technology (LET) Lab, within the Learning and Learning Processes (LLP) Research Unit at the Faculty of Education and Psychology, conducts multidisciplinary research on learning, teaching, and technology-enhanced learning. Its work focuses on areas such as learning sciences, self- and socially shared regulation of learning, collaborative learning, emerging technologies, and data-driven approaches to understanding and supporting learning across educational contexts. About the job The positions are part of the Research Council of Finland funded project “Human-AI Shared Regulation of Learning: Preparing Higher Education Students to Learn and Work with AI (HAI-Learning)” (370619), led by Associate Professor Andy Nguyen. You will conduct doctoral research on human–AI shared regulation of learning, investigating how higher education students learn and work with AI. You will use advanced analytical methods, including multimodal and AI-driven learning analytics, to investigate human learning processes and contribute to the design and development of socio-technical systems for hybrid intelligence. You will work within a multidisciplinary team, contribute to project-related tasks, and publish and disseminate your findings in leading international scientific journals and conferences. What we offer The support of an experienced and enthusiastic team, with whom you can share your expertise and grow as an expert. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits. Development and career options of the big organization. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us . Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu. Who are you? In order to succeed and enjoy the position, we require from you: You must have a Master's degree in learning sciences or computer science, or in a relevant field, that was awarded not more than five years ago A transdisciplinary research orientation with demonstrated research experience or interest. A team player spirit with solid research and development skills. We expect candidates to demonstrate a willingness to engage in the study of both human learning processes and the design and development of AI systems. Experience with educational technology and/or software design and development. Excellent written and interpersonal communication skills in English. You must apply for the right to study for a doctoral degree at the beginning of your employment in accordance with the requirements of the University of Oulu Graduate School (UniOGS). We also appreciate Finnish language skills Proficiency in Python and C#, with experience developing XR applications, particularly Mixed Reality (MR) applications using Unity. Salary We are recruiting 1–2 doctoral researchers for fixed-term appointments, starting on 1 January 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter , with the following contract periods: Position 1: until 31 August 2029. Position 2, if appointed: until 31 December 2028. The salary will be based on the levels 2-4 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary will be approx. 2600-3200 € per month (before taxes).  A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 25.10.2026 (23:59 Finnish local time) through our recruitment system. The application should be written in English and include the following: Cover letter CV following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity Publication List The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. The shortlisted candidates will also be asked to submit their diplomas, and their references will be contacted. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact Associate Professor Andy Nguyen, Faculty of Education and Psychology, LLP research Unit, andy.nguyen@oulu.fi Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/601 Published 08.Oct.2026 Last application date 25.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    }
  },
